Subject: [PATCH] staging: octeon: expose per-port OF node on netdev

The legacy Octeon Ethernet driver already resolves the device-tree node
for each hardware port and stores it in struct octeon_ethernet. The
net_device itself remains associated only with the shared PIP platform
device, so consumers such as DSA cannot resolve an ethernet phandle to a
specific Octeon master netdev.

Associate the net_device with the per-port OF node discovered by the
driver. This fixes the driver/OF association at its source and does not
add any B53-, board-name-, or OpenWrt-specific fallback.

--- a/drivers/staging/octeon/ethernet.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/octeon/ethernet.c
@@ -826,2 +826,4 @@ static int cvm_oct_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
+			dev->dev.of_node = priv->of_node;
+
 			INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&priv->port_periodic_work,
